{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017SfWwvGze8H5Naq1iQu4My","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Warmups lane codec library: every day's line codec as an exact ENCODER + decoder, plus a broad try-list of classical\nencoders for identifying an unknown day's codec from its Single Solve.\n\nWarmups (D1-D15): each Single is one sentence -- \"Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer to\nthe Game Master: <slug>\" -- under ONE codec that changes daily; Mastery day N = 5N-2 sets of N numbered lines, line k\nunder day k's codec, the sentence cut mid-word (reference/techniques/warmups.md). The encoders below reproduce the GM's\nbytes exactly (all 819 lines of D13 auto-mastery-d1a77831: lowercase hex/%xx, space-separated 8-bit binary, decimal,\n3-digit octal, decimal `&#NN;`, quoted lowercase `\\\\u00xx`, padded base32, unpadded base64url, ...), so\nhctf/today_probe.py can re-encode yesterday's verified Mastery sentence with TODAY's codec on a new last line and test\nthe solver BEFORE the Mastery clock (D12/D13: the first Mastery attempt failed on exactly that mix).\n\n  DAYS        [(day, name, enc, dec, free)] -- free = no alphabet signature (told apart only by how English it reads)\n  CANDIDATES  [(name, enc, dec|None)] -- DAYS first, then format variants, classical ciphers and chained pairs\n  infer(plain, blob, hints=())  -> (name, enc) | None: the encoder E with E(plain) == blob.strip() (or dec(blob) == plain)\n  plaintext(blob, slug)         -> the decoded sentence (decode_chunk -> peel -> candidate decoders -> template)\n\nAlso registers SPECULATIVE keyless free-text decoders with lib.decode.register_free (day=None): lib.decode's joint\nfree-line assignment tries them only for a blob with more free lines than the confirmed free codecs cover AND more lines\nthan the newest confirmed codec's day -- never on D1-D13 bytes. Pure stdlib.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport binascii\nimport codecs\nimport collections\nimport functools\nimport gzip\nimport html\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport quopri\nimport os\nimport re\nimport string\nimport time\nimport unicodedata\nimport urllib.parse\nimport zlib\n\nSENTENCE = \"Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer to the Game Master: {slug}\"\nSLUG = re.compile(r\"[a-z]+(?:-[a-z]+)+-\\d{2,}\")\n\n\ndef _u(s):\n    return s.encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef _t(b):\n    return b.decode(\"utf-8\") if isinstance(b, (bytes, bytearray)) else b\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ day codecs (exact)\ndef rot(s, n):\n    return \"\".join(chr((ord(c) - 97 + n) % 26 + 97) if \"a\" <= c <= \"z\" else\n                   chr((ord(c) - 65 + n) % 26 + 65) if \"A\" <= c <= \"Z\" else c for c in s)\n\n\ndef atbash(s):\n12:  DAYS        [(day, name, enc, dec, free)] -- free = no alphabet signature (told apart only by how English it reads)\n17:Also registers SPECULATIVE keyless free-text decoders with lib.decode.register_free (day=None): lib.decode's joint\n18:free-line assignment tries them only for a blob with more free lines than the confirmed free codecs cover AND more lines\n149:    \"\"\"(name, enc, dec, free) of a known day's line codec, or None.\"\"\"\n150:    for d, name, enc, dec, free in DAYS:\n152:            return name, enc, dec, free\n192:# lib.ciphers.morse_decode, which drops punctuation (the slug hyphen `-....-`). Case is lost, so morse_free also offers\n227:def morse_free(p):\n329:# Morse carrying another codec (D16 \"Dot Com\" = Morse over hex): Morse loses case, so the inner codec is a case-free\n412:    \"\"\"[(inner, text)] for Morse (strict `.-`, else any 2-symbol alphabet) carrying a case-free inner codec, best\n437:    \"\"\"The text under Morse-over-<case-free codec>, else None.\"\"\"\n442:def morse_layer_free(p):\n502:def morse_timing_free(p):\n513:# column) or decimal 0-31. Case-free, so it can also carry hex (FIGS digits + LTRS A-F). US-TTY differs only in\n548:    \"\"\"ITA2 of s (or of the case-free inner codec's text, e.g. inner=\"hex\"): fmt bin (5-bit groups), tape (`*`/`.`)\n624:    \"\"\"[(variant, text)] for an ITA2 blob, best first: a case-free inner codec under it (hex first) when the\n660:def baudot_free(p):\n693:# case-free inner layer (hex digits, decimal / octal / binary codes, base32, A1Z26) when the spelled string isn't text.\n749:    \"\"\"[(inner, text)] for a strict NATO fragment, best first: a case-free inner layer (hex first) when the spelled\n776:def nato_layer_free(p):\n416:FREE_CODECS = ((\"rot\", 2), (\"rev\", 12), (\"atb\", 13), (\"caesar7\", 14),   # D14: fixed Caesar +7 (decode rot-7)\n417-               (\"rot47\", 15),   # D15: ROT47 over printable ASCII 33-126 (self-inverse)\n418-               (\"rail\", 18))    # D18: 3-rail fence (offset 0) first, then lib.warmups_codecs.rail_free's other fences\n419-_SLUG_END = re.compile(r\"[a-z]+(?:-[a-z]+)+-\\d{2,}\\s*$\")\n420-_D2 = re.compile(r\"\\d\\d\")\n421-# The GM's slug is adj-noun-noun-NN: a 3-word slug end outranks a 2-word one (D14 Mastery set22: rev/atb swapped on\n422-# lines 12/13 still ended in a 2-word 'x-yyyy...-NN' tail and out-scored the true slug on bigrams).\n--\n424:# Free-text codec registry [(name, day, cands_fn(fragment) -> [decoded candidates])], FREE_CODECS first. A new day's\n425-# keyless free-text codec is one register_free(name, day, fn) call (the ratchet / a generalize worker adds it). day=None\n426-# = SPECULATIVE (lib.warmups_codecs.SPECULATIVE_FREE: rot47, swapcase, per-word reversal, ...): tried only for a blob\n427-# with more lines than the newest confirmed day and ONE free line the confirmed codecs can't cover (a new day's codec\n428-# nobody registered yet) -- never on D1-D13 bytes.\n429-_FREE = []\n430-# lib.decode strict branches beyond D1-D13 (morse, a1z26): 0 historic warmups fragments match (tests/test_day14_s2.py).\n--\n465:for _n, _d in [(n, d) for n, d in FREE_C