{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM91sXfq9LRhJWqkmUon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two day-24 facts are now in lib/, and the ratchet gate is green (`python3 -m hctf.orchestrate ratchet-gate day24`).\n\n1. **Metadata: `evtx.record_count` is now verified for day 24.** The prebuilt `record_value` extractor counts the records it finds in every chunk of the file, not the \"next record id\" stored in the file header. It matched the GM on all 10 cases (3 on the single, 43 on the TT, 9 to 119 across the 8 Mastery sets). The verified entry goes through a new wrapper, `lib/meta/evtx.py`, because the gate doesn't allow a verified entry to point straight into `prebuilt/`. I removed the key from the prebuilt `evtx.py` FIELDS.\n2. **Warmups: the day-24 netstring codec is added.** Each character is written as `1:c,`. I added it as entry 24 in `lib/warmups_codecs.py` `DAYS` with an exact encoder and a strict decoder (`netstr_dec`). I also added a branch for it to `lib.decode.decode_chunk`. The encoder reproduces the single, the TT and all 118 Mastery line-24s byte for byte, and `decode_chunked` now solves all 118 Mastery sets. It isn't a free-text codec, so nothing went into `FREE_CODECS`.\n3. **A speed fix I made without being asked.** On the first gate run, the meta lane solver took 1.03 s on the day-24 Mastery case, over its 1 s budget. Half of that was `lib.meta` parsing all 1.8 MB of prebuilt modules on import. `_prebuilt_fields` now parses only the `FIELDS = {...}` statement and falls back to the full parse if that fails. Import time dropped from 0.51 s to 0.18 s, and the registry (12,990 keys) and conflict list are identical to before.\n4. **Tests:** I added checks to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py` for the netstring codec, the verified evtx count (on a small hand-built EVTX file), and that the faster FIELDS read gives the same result as a full parse for every prebuilt module. I didn't change any exis